                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [
                    {
                      "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                      "Text": "Potential branching rate is determined by the commonly observed pattern of tillering in wheat, in which each tiller emerges with the third leaf on its parent axis (e.g. first tiller emerges at the same time as the third leaf on the main stem, the first secondary tiller appears with the third leaf on tiller 1).  This is described as a simple function of main stem leaf number. This function is varied occasionally between Oat cultivars due to the wide range of plant habits.",
